@startuml
!theme plain
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowColor #475569
title Codex Review - Scope, Execution, Assessment and Recovery

start
:PR published; worktree clean\nRefresh actual PR base; resolve base/head SHAs;
:Acquire worktree review lock\nRead local saved state;
if (Active runner or possible orphan child?) then (yes)
  :Report existing state/log\nInspect exact process; do not duplicate;
  stop
else (no)
endif
if (Same base/head execution completed\nand no --force-full?) then (yes)
  :Reuse saved execution + log\nRead existing assessment or assess pending result;
else (no)
  if (--incremental explicitly selected\nPrevious review assessed pass/blocking\nSame base; previous head is ancestor\nDifferent current head; no --force-full?) then (yes)
    :Review base = previous assessed head\nAll intervening commits are included;
    note right
      Main agent must establish bounded fix impact.
      Interfaces / security boundaries / cross-module
      behavior / uncertainty require full coverage.
      Previous findings are verified separately.
    end note
  else (no)
    :Review base = actual PR base\nFull PR coverage;
  endif
  :Archive previous record\nSave running state + scope + head + log path;
  :Invoke built-in codex review --base <resolved SHA>\nStream output to terminal and local log;
  note right
    Every 5 min: elapsed + output-idle notice.
    After 15 min: inspect progress / error evidence.
    Silence alone is not proof of failure.
    No blind retry or automatic timeout pass.
  end note
  if (Exit zero AND same head AND clean worktree?) then (yes)
    :Execution completed\nAssessment remains pending;
  else (no)
    :Record incomplete / interrupted\nRetain log and failure evidence;
    :Resolve environment/error; retry explicitly\nCurrent runner falls back to full review\nwhen latest saved run is unassessed;
    stop
  endif
endif
:Main agent reads complete conclusion\nChecks original findings + affected test evidence;
if (Complete conclusion with no blockers?) then (yes)
  :Record pass + evidence note\nVerify PR head and required checks before merge;
  stop
else (no)
  if (Confirmed blocking findings?) then (yes)
    :Record blocking + evidence note\nBatch fixes -> affected tests -> applicable redaction\nCommit -> push -> select next review scope;
    stop
  else (missing conclusion)
    :Do not record pass\nDiagnose and rerun with --force-full if needed;
    stop
  endif
endif
@enduml
